      "textEn": "275\n\nThey were adorned with Karadhani. The one who shakes the breasts with the twinkling of the stars,\nWith excellent necklaces and ornaments, at every step. Like a reflected light, moving in the middle,\nIt moves the waves of the shore, one after another. 19. Meaning of the word\n\nAavartan—falling down; Udvartan—and jumping up; Kampita—shaking; Stana—of both breasts; Prakrishta—beautiful; Haar—of necklace; Uru-bharaih—due to the weight of the thigh; Pade Pade—on every step; Prabhajyamanaam Iv—as if it will break; Madhyatha—in the middle part of the body; Chalat—like this, shaking and swaying; Pada-pravalam—red-red feet like a peacock; Nayatiem—fickle; Tat Tat—\nHere and there. Because the ball was bouncing up and down, when she played with it, her breasts would move.\nAnd when she walked here and there with her moongo-like red, soft feet, the weight of those breasts,\nand the heavy garland of flowers, her waist seemed to be breaking at every step. Dixu bhramatkandukapalairbhrusham\nPradwignatarayatalolalochanam.\nAdorned with earrings, shining with self-earned glory,\nAdorned with the lotus-like face of the forehead. 20. Meaning of the word\n\nDikshu—in all directions; bhramat—jumping; kanduk—ball; chaplaih—agility; bhrusham—now and then; prodhigya—full of worry; tara—eyes; ayat—widely open; lol—restless; lochanam—with eyes; swa-karna—in both ears;\nvibhrajita—radiant; kundal—earring; ulasat—shining; kapol—cheek; neel—dark; alak—with hair\nattached; mandit—beautifully adorned; aananam—face..\n\nThat woman's face was broad and beautiful, and she was adorned with restless eyes, and she\nwas spinning with the ball thrown by her hands. Her ears had two shining earrings.\nHer cheeks were adorned with a dark shadow, and the hair scattered on her face made her even more beautiful to look at. Shlathaddukulam kabarim cha vichutam\nSannahyati vamakaren valluguna. They delude the lotus-like one with various obstacles.\nThey delude the world with the illusion of the self. 21."
