      "textEn": "293\n\nTritiyam Vadvameke Tasam Sangnasutastrayah. Yama, Yami, listen to the Shraddha of the gods and the sons. 9. Meaning of the word\n\nTritiyam—third wife; Vadvam—Vadva; Eke—some people; Tasam—out of the three wives; Sangya-sutah—three children of Sangya; Yamah—one son Yam; Yami—daughter Yami; Shraddhadevah—second son Shraddhadev; Chhayaah—of the shadow; Cha—and;\nSutan—to the sons; Shrunu—listen. It is said that Surya Deva also had a third wife whose name was Vadva. Of these, three wives, Sansa had three children—Yam, Yami and Shraddhadeva. Now I will describe the shadow's\ndescendants. Savarnistapati Kanya Bharatiya Sanvarasya Ya. The third of the Shani constellation are the twin sons of Vadava. 10. Meaning of the word\n\nSavarnih—Savarni; Tapati—Tapati; Kanya—Daughter; Barya—Wife; Sanvaranasya—Of King Sanvarana; Ya—Who; Shanai-sharah—\nShanai-sharah; Tritiya—Third offspring; Abhut—Born; Ashwinau—Both Ashwini Kumaras; Vadva-atma-jau—Wife named Vadva\nson of.\n.\n\nChhaya had a son Savarni and a daughter Tapati, who later became the wife of King Sanvaran. The third child of Chhaya is said to be Shaneshchar (Saturn). Vadva gave birth to two sons whose names are\nAshwini-Bandhu. In the eighth, the difference is that the Savarna has come.  11. Meaning of the word.\n\nIn the eighth—eighth; in the intervals—in the intervals; came—on coming; Savarani—Savarani; will be—will become; Manu—eighth Manu;\nNirmok—Nirmok; Virajask-Aadya—Virajask etc.; Savarani—Of Savarani; Tanaya—Son; Nripa—Oh King. Your Highness! When the eighth Manu's time comes, Savarni Manu will be formed. Nirmok, Virjask etc.\nWill be his sons. Note: It is the reign of Vaivasvata Manu. According to astrological calculations, we are in the twenty-eighth era of Vaivasvata Manu. Each Manu lives for seventy-one eras, and in one day of Brahmaji, such fourteen\nManus govern. At this time, we are in the era of the seventh Manu, Vaivasvata, and the eighth Manu will be after millions of years"
